{
  "case_id": "2018-18-459",
  "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit in this case recognized an unprecedented inferred private right to recover for negligent violations of Section 14(e) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934.\nFor two independent reasons, we would ask this Court to reverse that decision.\nFirst, as the government itself recognizes, this Court's precedents compel the conclusion that Section 14(e) does not confer any implied private right at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Garre, why should we consider that when it wasn't raised in this case until, what was it, the motion for rehearing in the court of appeals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because Sandoval, if you continue down to the end of that paragraph on Cannon, said context is relevant, but it's only relevant as it informs text. And there's nothing about the context of Borak or 14(a) that informs 14(e) because 14(e) is written completely different than 14(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can I get your broader argument --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Sandoval answers that by saying statutory context informs -- is relevant as it informs text. But I think the broader point here is that this Court has been -- made very clear that when it comes to recognizing implied private rights, this is a very special, perilous endeavor, and so there are very explicit limits on when the Court is going to do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I'd like you to tell me, do I understand you right to say not even the SEC would have a right to sue for negligence under 14(e), not even the SEC?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you answer Justice Breyer's point, which is -- I -- I took his point to be that since 14(e) borrows the language of 10-5, and we have all along interpreted 10b-5 to require scienter, why shouldn't we require the same standard here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Although we submit only one question is properly presented, this entire dispute can be resolved looking to this Court's usual tools of statutory construction and the text, context, purpose, and history of Section 14(e)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's no private right of action in the text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our argument is that looking to the specifics of Section 14(e), the text that Congress uses, the context in which they used it, the entire point was to harmonize 14(e) with 14(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What about Central Bank? I mean, one response could be don't repeat that again, but do you have any other response to their -- their raising of Central Bank?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you do with Ms. Ratner's distinction of Cannon?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "04b51750f422c8f96391e8a358f1d4ef6ba9d4278664c06e690160e5c109aa39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-04b51750f422-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you -- are you sure about that? I mean, that seems --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2018-18-459",
      "confidence": 0.0,
